,"position":{"commit_sha":"1abc78c37a03212d497924b1c820345948d41efc","position":"1785410507855204001-f23eab1d-597b-49d5-be98-544b86009b77"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"10f931a99b22217630efde814ddb09395fa3d8459badcd3aab4f495a16a79312","event_uuid":"c9e65c9c-9a3e-469d-bb09-3ecc3b0dfbe8","position":{"commit_sha":"1abc78c37a03212d497924b1c820345948d41efc","position":"1785410508376283001-c9e65c9c-9a3e-469d-bb09-3ecc3b0dfbe8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"073c7bec14f2b0d4e306dbe7bf7ec169af05dfa1e861782a6e383a6d46803583","event_uuid":"d51e262a-85c8-415d-a4bb-e76e7fc75a6d","position":{"commit_sha":"d80baa4089aab83d659fe03adb2f5f345925aaf2","position":"1785410760513737239-d51e262a-85c8-415d-a4bb-e76e7fc75a6d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[],"created_at":1785384361946852001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ee92b3c6-77d9-4f7e-8644-014345cb6e34","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d52a-40cd-75d4-46cb"},{"link_uuid":"3154faec-9291-42e3-b010-85df92d397b2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8a62-24f3-f2f7-4649"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nPass-1 submits every chunk and AGENT future at once into a 6-wide pool (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:438,462-464); with a cold cache the first ~6 concurrent calls each pay a full cache-WRITE for the byte-identical plan-bearing system prefix — measured shape ~7.9N effective plan-tokens versus an ideal 2.15N (~3.7x). The warm-then-fan-out pattern already exists, proven, for container bins (pass1.py:184-232, gated on CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS=4096 and >=2 pairings, with graceful degradation on a failed warm).\n\n## Approach\nPort the container warm gate to the main pool: when the estimated shared-prefix tokens >= CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS and (chunks + agent criteria) >= 2, run the first single-turn chunk to completion serially (writing the cache prefix), then submit the remainder to the pool; a non-systemic warm failure degrades to direct fan-out exactly as the container path does (pass1.py:203-212). Verification uses the per-call cache metrics landed by the usage-instrumentation story. Alternative rejected: serializing the whole pool — forfeits 6-way parallelism to save only the redundant writes the single warm call already eliminates.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py, tests/llm/test_pass1_warmup.py.\n\n## Testing\nUnit with a recording FakeRunner: with the gate met, exactly one call completes before any pool submission and the rest fan out; below the token gate or with a single call, behavior is unchanged; a warm-call exception falls back to direct fan-out and the review completes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With >= 2 Pass-1 calls and a large plan, the first call completes before the pool starts (checked: unit test asserting call-ordering via a recording runner).\n- [ ] Small plans and single-call reviews bypass the warm-up (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] A failing warm call degrades to today's direct fan-out and the review still completes (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] In a stubbed-usage run, the shared prefix incurs one cache write and N-1 cache reads (checked: unit test over the per-call usage records from the instrumentation seam).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py","reason":"warm-then-fan-out for main pool"},{"path":"tests/llm/test_pass1_warmup.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","d52a-40cd-75d4-46cb"],["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","8a62-24f3-f2f7-4649"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"f23eab1d-597b-49d5-be98-544b86009b77","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"25fa-0865-8b61-498c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Warm-then-fan-out for the Pass-1 chunk and agent pool","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3a0a0b31-dbbe-4df2-beee-a9a057872e5a","5ae1090c-0c7b-44c1-af7e-05a1db963a7d","ee92b3c6-77d9-4f7e-8644-014345cb6e34","4898ac52-fb8f-409e-9ed4-d95887c4cd52","f23eab1d-597b-49d5-be98-544b86009b77","c9e65c9c-9a3e-469d-bb09-3ecc3b0dfbe8","d51e262a-85c8-415d-a4bb-e76e7fc75a6d","3154faec-9291-42e3-b010-85df92d397b2"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785423362134788223,"uuid":"48de5301-c453-4a6a-a9cf-980949e1ca60"}